course: dictionary
lesson: 1717
title: Words that wrap around: circumpolar
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Circumpolar is built from two parts you may know. Circum means around, and polar means to do with a pole, the ends of the Earth. So circumpolar means found around a pole. «The Antarctic Circumpolar Current flows round Antarctica» tells you the current goes all the way around that icy continent.
explain: Use the context to check your meaning. The sentence is about an ocean current that is the strongest in the world, carrying many times more water than all the world's rivers together. Circumpolar is not describing something small or local. It describes something huge that goes around a pole.
explain: The same word also works in the night sky. The Plough is circumpolar from the UK, so it never sets below the horizon but circles around the pole star. Context helps again: the same word can describe a current in the sea or a group of stars.
fact: Circumpolar means found around the North Pole or South Pole, or living in the regions near them.
fact: Circum means around, and polar means to do with a pole.
fact: «The Antarctic Circumpolar Current flows round Antarctica» and is the strongest ocean current in the world.
fact: In astronomy, circumpolar describes a star that never sets below the horizon from a certain place but circles the pole star.
fact: Phrases to notice: «circumpolar stars», «circumpolar current», «circumpolar peoples».
exercise: «The Antarctic Circumpolar Current flows round Antarctica.» What does circumpolar mean here? | Moving very fast along the coast | Lying deep under the sea | Very cold and icy | *Going around the South Pole
exercise: Circumpolar is built from two parts. Which part means around? | polar | pol | cir | *circum
exercise: In astronomy, what does a circumpolar star do from the UK? | Falls below the horizon every night | Only shines in summer | *Circles the pole star and never sets | Shoots across the sky and disappears by morning
test: «Circumpolar peoples live near the North or South Pole.» What does circumpolar describe here? | Found in hot deserts near the equator | Found only in deep oceans | *Found near the North or South Pole | Found on high mountains far from the sea
test: Is the Plough circumpolar from the UK? | Only in winter | No, it sets every night | *Yes, it circles the pole star and never sets | Only in the southern sky
exam: What does circumpolar mean? | Moving very fast across the sky | Found only in the middle of the ocean | *Found around a pole, or a star that circles the pole and never sets | Very cold and very windy
